# The monorepo's own .gitignore covers all of this, but `git subtree split` exports this
# folder alone: the root's rules do not travel with it.
#
# And Steam does not read .gitignore at all. SteamUGC.SetItemContent takes the junction's
# target directory exactly as it stands on disk, with no filtering, so anything sitting in
# the published folder is published. That is what `Mod/` is for: the junction points there,
# and the docs and this file stay out of reach by construction.

# Claude Code session worktrees and local settings: each worktree is a full copy of the
# monorepo, hundreds of megabytes, and they are never shared.
.claude/

# Development environments.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user

# System.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
